  "what_it_would_authorise": "exactly one execution of v26c_j21_training_ready_attestation.py --execute, which writes ONE leaf containing a result, a receipt and a commit verification. It launches nothing.",
  "what_j21_is": "a READ-ONLY evidence aggregation over J19A, J19B, J19C, K1R1, the J20 critic-only warm-up and the J20 R3 restore audit. It reads committed artefacts, re-hashes every pinned byte and evaluates eighteen binding gates. It imports the standard library and nothing else: no train_ppo_mlp, no Ray, no torch, no OpenSim, no simulation module. It starts no Ray, builds no Algorithm, constructs no environment, launches no subprocess, samples nothing, rolls out nothing and trains nothing. Gate T14 audits its own source at run time.",
  "what_rev1_corrects": [
    "T15 no longer claims that no upstream promotion occurred. J19A legitimately promoted an ACTOR; the gate now checks only that no upstream stage promoted THIS J20 checkpoint to TRAINING_INPUT_ONLY, claimed checkpoint training readiness, or authorised a launch.",
